{"title":"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the radius of a circle is a rational number, its area is given by a number which is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4148bb4c0b271d2abe43dcecaae35ee7b1c5862e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)\\ } \\text{rational}  \\qquad \\textbf{(B)\\ } \\text{irrational} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)\\ } \\text{integral} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)\\ } \\text{a perfect square }\\qquad \\textbf{(E)\\ } \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"703\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the radius of the circle be the common fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/818eea6f26c85d8168247bb918664669cc943923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"17\" height=\"33\" /> Then the area of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780e70c23059e18f9374abbc095572c7227eea76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi \\cdot \\frac{a^2}{b^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"39\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> is irrational and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d61dba2e4b918cb0df217e5ebfcb8c043daf8a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^2}{b^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"19\" height=\"39\" /> is rational, their product must be irrational. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0cdd2d628e533bf874621ae1b229985f8e2996d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"33\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The phrasing of the problem makes it clear that the rule would apply to all rational radii. So let r be equal to one. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> times 1 squared is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> which is irrational. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/c/a0cdd2d628e533bf874621ae1b229985f8e2996d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"33\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~YJC64002776\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME\" title=\"1952 AHSME\">1952 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1952 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1952\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1952 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1952_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" 